      "description": "Detroit techno emerged in the mid-80s from Belleville Three (Juan Atkins, Derrick May, Kevin Saunderson), fusing Kraftwerk's precision with Parliament-Funkadelic's soul. The sound is mechanical yet emotional\\u2014cold synthesizers carrying warm melodies. The kick is punchy but not overwhelming, usually a tight 909 with moderate decay around 0.3-0.4, tuned neutral or slightly up. Snares crack cleanly on 2 and 4, often with a short reverb tail. Hi-hats drive the track with steady 16ths, closed hats dominant with open hats accenting the offbeats sparingly.",
      "production": "The bassline is the soul\\u2014deep, melodic, often a sawtooth or square wave filtered to sit warm in the low-mids. Detroit bass moves, it's not a static root note. Chord stabs punctuate with string-like pads or Rhodes-style keys, heavy on the minor 7ths and 9ths for that bittersweet futurism. The mix is spacious\\u2014every element has room to breathe. Reverb is used tastefully, never washing things out. The feel is driving but sophisticated, like a machine dreaming of being human.",
