      "description": "Electro is the original electronic street music\\u2014born from hip-hop, raised on Kraftwerk, defined by the TR-808. Afrika Bambaataa's 'Planet Rock' in 1982 fused German electronics with Bronx attitude and created a new form. The 808 is essential: that deep, booming kick that rattles trunks, the snappy electronic snare, the metallic cowbell that became electro's signature. The tempo is slower than house or techno, usually 110-120, giving room for the funk to breathe.",
      "production": "The rhythm is syncopated and funky\\u2014not four-on-the-floor but broken patterns with kicks landing on the one and off-beats. The snare typically cracks on two and four but with ghost notes and rolls adding complexity. The cowbell drives the track, often on every quarter note or in syncopated patterns. Claps layer with snares for thickness. The bass is huge and subby, often simple octave patterns but tuned to shake foundations. Synth leads are robotic and melodic\\u2014often monophonic arpeggios or single-note hooks. Vocoder vocals add to the mechanical human hybrid aesthetic. The feel is futuristic retro\\u2014what 1982 thought 2000 would sound like.",
