      "description": "Jungle is drum and bass's rawer, more soulful ancestor\\u2014before the genre got streamlined, when the breaks were chopped rougher and the samples pulled from reggae, ragga, and soul. The Amen break is king here, timestretched and pitch-shifted into new forms, the snare hits crunchy and distorted rather than clean. The tempo is slightly slower than modern D&B, giving more room for the ragga vocals and dub influences. This is sound system music\\u2014designed for massive bass bins.",
      "production": "The breaks are treated more aggressively\\u2014timestretching creates artifacts that become part of the sound, giving that characteristic crunchy, gritty texture. Snare rolls are constant, creating the 'rollers' feel that defines the genre. The bass is often a reese\\u2014a detuned sawtooth creating that growling, moving texture that became jungle's signature. Samples from reggae and dancehall tracks are chopped and looped, often pitching vocals up to create the 'chipmunk' effect. Heavy use of delay and reverb on snares creates space and depth. The overall mix is muddier than modern D&B, warmer, more chaotic\\u2014sound system music that prioritizes impact over clarity.",
