          "decay": 0.08,
          "level": 0.4,
          "note": "The TRIPLET HI-HAT is footwork's rhythmic fingerprint. Rather than straight 16ths, the hats play patterns that imply triplet subdivisions \\u2014 groups of 3 over the 4/4 grid. In a 16-step sequencer this is approximated by unevenly spaced hits that create a loping, rolling feel. Think of it as 12/8 time superimposed on 4/4. Velocity variation is crucial \\u2014 accented hits on the triplet downbeats with ghost notes between. The pattern shown is an approximation; in practice, producers program these by feel in piano roll, not step sequencer, placing hats on exact triplet grid positions."
