      "lineage": "### Genesis: From Ghetto House to Footwork\\nJuke/Footwork emerged from Chicago's ghetto house scene when pioneering DJs began playing records at 45 RPM instead of 33 RPM, creating an urgent, hyperkinetic sound. The genre crystallized between 1996-1998 through three foundational figures:",
      "currentScene": "### Chicago: Post-Rashad Era\\nFollowing DJ Rashad's death in 2014, Chicago's scene has struggled with:\\nYouth migration to drill music: Local preference shifting away from footwork\\nVenue closures: Underground spaces becoming scarce\\nEconomic pressures: Gentrification affecting core communities\\nTeklife continuity: DJ Spinn, DJ Taye maintaining legacy"
