          "distortion": 0.05,
          "note": "Four-on-the-floor but SOFT. This is not a pounding techno kick \\u2014 it's a gentle, steady pulse that anchors the floating delays. Tight, clean, round. 909-style with the tone rolled off, or a deeper, softer kick sample. Short decay so it doesn't compete with the sub-bass or the low end of the delayed chords. Often slightly low-passed to remove click and high transient \\u2014 the kick should feel like a heartbeat in the distance, not a punch in the chest. Volume lower than in standard techno \\u2014 maybe -6dB below the chord/delay textures."
