          "note": "Four-on-the-floor \\u2014 the metronomic backbone. Unlike house or techno, the kuduro kick is NOT the star \\u2014 it's the grid reference for the percussion chaos above. Tight, clipped, punchy, with short decay. Almost toy-like in some productions \\u2014 thin and snappy rather than deep and booming. Some Lisbon batida variants drop the kick to half-time or use broken patterns, but canonical Angolan kuduro keeps the four-on-the-floor steady."
