          "note": "THE tresillo pattern \\u2014 the rhythmic heart of kuduro. This snare (or rimshot/sidestick) hits the first two pulses of the tresillo in each half-bar: steps 3 and 6 in the first half (3+3 grouping), steps 11 and 14 in the second half. Against the four-on-the-floor kick, this creates the characteristic lurching, syncopated groove. Dry, cracking, bright \\u2014 no reverb. Some productions use a clap or rimshot instead."
