          "distortion": 0.15,
          "note": "The dembow tresillo kick \\u2014 the DNA of reggaeton. This is a doubled 3+3+2 pattern across the 16-step bar: steps 0, 3, 6 (first tresillo: 3+3+2) then 8, 11, 14 (second tresillo: 3+3+2). The kick hits create an uneven, propulsive rhythm that drives the body forward. The sound is a punchy, tight 808-style kick \\u2014 not the long-sustaining 808 bass hit (that's the bass synth), but a short, clipped kick with moderate attack and short decay. Some modern productions simplify to just steps 0, 6, 8, 14 or even sparser patterns, but the full tresillo-doubled pattern shown here is the canonical dembow. Clean, punchy, not overly distorted \\u2014 the distortion lives on the 808 bass, not the kick."
